@meta
id: 26-06
title: One line, and then the same again
chapter: 26
type: lesson
skills: filter-bang
par: 27
minutes: 5
vscode: retype both lines in capitals
open: api-notes.md

@brief
Two lines in this document list values in lower case. The API returns
them in upper case, and the document is meant to match the API.

`tr a-z A-Z` is the shell's shortest way of saying "upper case this".
Feed it one line at a time.

There is a shorthand for the line the cursor is on, the same shape as
`dd` and `yy`: doubling the operator means "this line". And a filter, like
any other change, is repeatable.

@keys
| `!!cmd` | filter the current line — short for `!_cmd` |
| `!3jcmd` | filter this line and the three below it |
| `.` | repeat the last filter on the line the cursor is now on |
| `tr a-z A-Z` | upper case everything on standard input |

@hints
Get to the first lower-case list, then double the bang.
--
`!!tr a-z A-Z` and Enter does the first one. Do not type the second one
out again.
--
`6G`, `!!tr a-z A-Z` Enter, `4j`, `.`, `:wq`.

@solution
    6G  !!tr a-z A-Z<Enter>  4j  .  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-two keystrokes, and the second line cost one of them.

`.` repeating a filter is the part worth keeping. Vim remembers the whole
command, so a fiddly `awk` one-liner typed once can be dropped onto line
after line with a single key — and if you want it on a run of lines
instead, `!3j` or `!}` does the run in one pass.

The counted form deserves a warning that the range form does not need.
`!5j` filters six lines, this one and five more, because `j` is a motion
and the operator covers the line you start on. If you miscount you do not
get an error, you get five lines through a command that was meant for
six. `!}` and `!ip` do not have that failure mode, which is why they are
the ones to reach for on anything with a shape.

@start api-notes.md
# Status values

The API returns every status in upper case. These two lines came out of
an old ticket and are still in lower case.

pending, shipped, cancelled, refunded

The refund states are tracked separately:

partial, full, rejected

@expected api-notes.md
# Status values

The API returns every status in upper case. These two lines came out of
an old ticket and are still in lower case.

PENDING, SHIPPED, CANCELLED, REFUNDED

The refund states are tracked separately:

PARTIAL, FULL, REJECTED
